1. Create the project
Open CMD and type:
cd Desktop
mkdir TomcatProject
cd TomcatProject
notepad index.html


Write the HTML code in Notepad, then save it.
<html>
<body>
<h1>Hello from Apache Tomcat!</h1>
<p>My DevOps Lab Program 3 is successful.</p>
</body>
</html>


2. Create the Dockerfile
notepad Dockerfile


Write and save this code:
FROM tomcat:10.1-jdk17-temurin
RUN rm -rf /usr/local/tomcat/webapps/*
COPY index.html /usr/local/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/index.html
EXPOSE 8080
CMD ["catalina.sh", "run"]

*
ren Dockerfile.txt Dockerfile

3. Build the Docker image
docker build -t tomcat-lab .


4. Check the image
docker images


Expected: tomcat-lab appears in the image list.
5. Run the container
docker run -d -p 8081:8080 --name tomcat-container tomcat-lab


We use port 8081 because port 8080 was already occupied on your laptop.
6. Check the running container
docker ps


Expected: tomcat-container shows a status of Up.
7. Display the webpage
Open Chrome and enter:
http://localhost:8081Expected output:
Hello from Apache Tomcat!
My DevOps Lab Program 3 is successful.
Result


docker login
docker tag tomcat-lab:latest dikkshitat/tomcat-lab:latest
docker push dikkshitat/tomcat-lab:latest
The Docker image was created successfully, and the HTML webpage was deployed and accessed through the Apache Tomcat container.
